**Definition 4.2 (exact M record orders and selection algorithm).** The
eight lists, in order, are acquisition, old ingress, new ingress,
installation, meter, cover/package, rights, frontier. Each cell record
is $[U(\mathrm{port}),U(\mathrm{creation\ position}),\mathrm{eight\ tracks}]$.
The complete body is the eight-field tuple whose field $i=0,\ldots,7$
is $[U(i),\operatorname{List}(\mathrm{records}_i)]$. Finite stage/type tags
use their first textual occurrence order in the native routine expansion;
absent/present alternatives use 0/1 followed by the present framed value.
Descriptor records retain their full actual fields, backing endpoints,
creation/origin and seal/availability values. Records are grouped by
structure, then physical port, then creation position, all in increasing
order. An absent constructed relation has an explicit empty list, not
an invented initialized record.

Acquisition records follow the original template/predecessor/fence chain
and include all backing referenced by its no-update rows in their original
field order. Old ingress records follow AIF Definition 2.3's actual serial
creation order. New ingress records follow the actual 38 append chain:
ignore its initial F; complete binary frame/F blocks precede the current
written block prefix. Installation records follow RCA Definition 14.2's
physical field order, with the leading F excluded; partial fields retain
their raw selected cells and actual construction stage. Its frozen binding
distinguishes this prefix from later stages. Meter records are all its
constructed cells in append order, including its current end and head
tracks. Cover/package records follow their declared archive/bank-copy
creation chains and include their raw selected partial material, not a
fictional shorter sealed object. Rights are the existing designated
token/availability slots with their absent/0/1 values. Frontier fields
have the declared stage, heads/cursors and optional pending bit order.

On a decoded raw record, implement this selection with ReadList/Nth, finite
tag tests, Find, unary cancellation, Take and append. Traverse a referenced
descriptor chain by its actual strictly earlier creation reference;
deduplicate selected cells by their port/creation pair and finally emit
them in the declared order. Each template identifies a finite number of
field roles; repeated descriptors and referenced finite context blocks
are list traversals, not a fixed-size snapshot. A current partial writer's
finite PC label identifies which declared fields and cells have already
been constructed. Reader-stage/marked-length scans delimit written data
before including it as consumed ingress. Unwritten initialized cells are
retained when they belong to selected raw backing, but are not consumed
input bits. Copies preserve origins; their local construction positions
remain distinct.

These are operations on an acquired representation. They do not read the
live meter to a moving end or confer a cross-owner graph traversal.

There is an explicit finite way to resolve a selected object's construction
role even when its descriptor or bank copy is incomplete. First run only
the basic acquisition/ingress/installation/meter/frontier scans needed for
PVC.6; they do not need any cover/package record. Replay those data for
the counted number of rows by Theorem 4.4. Fold its fixed program locations,
descriptor creations and backing-copy roles to mark the actual selected
cover/package cells, including an EX-created but not-yet-written current
cell. For bank backing, only fields designated as cover/package backing
are selected, with their actual field boundaries and completed or partial
version stage; unrelated register fields are excluded. Track those finite
role cases by native textual call site and represented bank field index,
using word lists for the unbounded marked occurrence set. The same fold
records seal/copy relations and rights at their actual rows. Project the
marked cells at the represented endpoint and emit the declared records.
This fold is a finite algorithm on a derived history, not an added history
coordinate of M. It compares no current live private state and consults
no Image block. It removes any need to guess a partial object's meaning
from unsealed payload bytes. The definition of M remains selection of
the existing objects and relations by their actual construction roles.

